+//    [Patch 0024 extends this to the COMPLETE bundle set of the Qt
+//    modules this executable links, so no bundle's presence ever
+//    again depends on an incidental reference. A full census of the
+//    Qt 6.9.3 iOS kit (the same aqt archives CI installs; bundle
+//    inventory from lib/objects-Release/*/qrc_*_init.cpp.o plus the
+//    framework symbol tables, compared against this executable's
+//    LC_SYMTAB) shows the linked modules carry exactly eight
+//    resource bundles: QtGui {gui_shaders, qpdf}, QtWidgets {qstyle,
+//    qstyle1, qstyle_fusion, qmessagebox}, QtPrintSupport
+//    {qprintdialog, qprintdialog1}. The v6 executable contained
+//    seven -- qprintdialog1 was missing, the same silent hole one
+//    level down (its data serves the generic print dialog's UI).
+//    All eight are now declared and called below. The census also
+//    closed two open questions: there is NO rhi_shaders bundle in
+//    this kit (QtGui ships exactly two resource objects), and PNG
+//    needs no plugin (Qt 6.9.3 builds the PNG handler into QtGui;
+//    the kit's imageformats are only gif/ico/jpeg/svg).]
 // 2) Environment defaults, set before QApplication exists.
 //    QT_WIDGETS_RHI=0 opts widget top-levels out of RHI-composited
